        <body>
            <div xml:id="d587">

                <pb facs="0956" n="836" xml:id="pg836"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">550.S1/327</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Switzerland (Riggs) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2750</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-10-29">October 29,
                        1932</date>.<lb/>[Received November 8.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith
                    Circular Letter No. 170 (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) dated October 28,
                        1932,<anchor n="22" xml:id="d587-f1"/> signed by Sir Eric Drummond, Secretary General of the League of Nations,
                    and referred to in the Legation’s telegram No. 85 of October 29, 11 a.m.,
                        1932.<anchor n="22" xml:id="d587-f2"/> This communication invites the United
                    States to be represented at the proposed Monetary and Economic Conference to be
                    held in London, the date of which will be decided by the Organizing Committee at
                    its session in November.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">B. Reath Riggs</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
